# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs: source, packaging
# metadata, and the README pyproject's [project] table points readme at. Nothing
# generated, nothing personal, and nothing that changes on every commit for a
# reason the image should not be rebuilt over (build artifacts, caches, test runs).

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
.git/
.github/

# Personal and machine-specific. Configuration reaches a container through
# --env-file or -e at run time, never baked into the image (janus/CLAUDE.md,
# no defaults for identity values).
.env
.claude/

# Generated or judge-facing artifacts with no bearing on what the image runs.
benchmarks/RESULTS.md
examples/
docs/
*.md
!README.md
